            {
                "entry_id": "3f979bd9-a1c1-3e2a-b5a8-4c1c5246df37",
                "word": "iconoclasme",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "5d1761df-0b36-4880-ba93-d1e1bb6b7d8c",
                        "entry_id": "3f979bd9-a1c1-3e2a-b5a8-4c1c5246df37",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "iconoclasmes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "05c68dc7-1aa9-3880-ad02-bd50c740ba13",
                        "entry_id": "3f979bd9-a1c1-3e2a-b5a8-4c1c5246df37",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Doctrine condamnant avec violence l'adoration des icônes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "772b8592-71ea-47a6-ac3f-0ccedec3d6a1",
                                "sense_id": "05c68dc7-1aa9-3880-ad02-bd50c740ba13",
                                "text": "André Grabar propose une interprétation de l'iconoclasme byzantin (728-843) en étudiant directement les œuvres d'art de l'époque de la persécution des images."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4cecf830-c55e-4814-82cd-f19075876821",
                                "sense_id": "05c68dc7-1aa9-3880-ad02-bd50c740ba13",
                                "text": "Certes, l’iconoclasme et l’aniconisme ne sont pas sans lien, mais la violence est propre à l’iconoclasme. Ainsi, l’on dira que l’islam est une religion aniconique, c’est-à-dire qui n’admet pas la représentation de Dieu, ni celle des êtres animés, et que les talibans afghans sont iconoclastes, parce qu’ils ont détruit de nombreuses images, dont les très célèbres Bouddhas de Bâmyân."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bdf1fab6-5684-4ddb-8996-43b5911a0fbe",
                        "source_entry_id": "3f979bd9-a1c1-3e2a-b5a8-4c1c5246df37",
                        "source_sense_id": "05c68dc7-1aa9-3880-ad02-bd50c740ba13",
                        "target_lang_word": "Bildersturm",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Bildersturm",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "debeda23-c9c6-37f4-9319-b61143dbee0b",
                                        "entry_id": "fafc6e70-5c85-3a8d-b865-101caf0c0160",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Zerstörung von Kirchenbildern"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "566d5dd9-7a6c-4740-9273-f25a6c5507fe",
                                                "sense_id": "debeda23-c9c6-37f4-9319-b61143dbee0b",
                                                "text": "Der Bildersturm forderte einen Großteil der Schönheit unserer Kathedrale."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "217739c1-cfc4-4dd2-ad13-c20eb402cfa0",
                                                "sense_id": "debeda23-c9c6-37f4-9319-b61143dbee0b",
                                                "text": "„Während des von Karlstadt angeheizten Wittenberger Bildersturms kam er von der Wartburg in die Stadt und predigte gegen pöbelhafte Rabatzmacherei.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "476d5872-672d-4366-86a3-70f635413eed",
                        "source_entry_id": "3f979bd9-a1c1-3e2a-b5a8-4c1c5246df37",
                        "source_sense_id": "05c68dc7-1aa9-3880-ad02-bd50c740ba13",
                        "target_lang_word": "Ikonoklasmus",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Ikonoklasmus",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "70924c45-9e73-3095-baa4-7871f4a58a43",
                                        "entry_id": "41eb8c7d-2faf-305d-bf3a-2f07c09a4590",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ablehnung und Zerstörung von Bildern (mit religiösem Wert)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3cd4daac-db74-4e6f-9bfa-d6f1a4f5f742",
                                                "sense_id": "70924c45-9e73-3095-baa4-7871f4a58a43",
                                                "text": "„Ikonoklasmus hatte im Dritten Reich natürlich eine stark antisemitische Komponente, Bilder von jüdischen Künstlern sowie Bücher von jüdischen Schriftstellern wurden verbrannt.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a189511-0447-4dda-bcdd-f20e2c355dad",
                                                "sense_id": "70924c45-9e73-3095-baa4-7871f4a58a43",
                                                "text": "„Erst mit der Überwindung des Ikonoklasmus erhielt die Ikone ihren heiligen Charakter, da man von da an zwischen der Darstellung und dem Dargestellten eine direkte Verbindung sah und letzterer ‚Energien‘ auf die Ikone herabsandte.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "76104593-df47-4215-89b5-2ac9d86d79f7",
                        "source_entry_id": "3f979bd9-a1c1-3e2a-b5a8-4c1c5246df37",
                        "source_sense_id": "05c68dc7-1aa9-3880-ad02-bd50c740ba13",
                        "target_lang_word": "iconoclasm",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "iconoclasm",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4971dcb6-4949-3032-8b91-f40f9ce1816d",
                                        "entry_id": "9bcf4a61-6ac6-3636-80e3-15d0431a86ed",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The belief in, participation in, or sanction of destroying religious icons and other symbols or monuments, usually with religious or political motives."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c0b2670f-1325-466f-a99b-07a92f13f12e",
                                                "sense_id": "4971dcb6-4949-3032-8b91-f40f9ce1816d",
                                                "text": "Finally, “iconoclasm” is a form of desecration and shares its general intention to deny the sacred qualities of an image and to demonstrate that it has no power, to prevent it from being treated as an idol or a rival to God.¹⁴ But not all forms of desecration constitute iconoclasm, though iconoclasm is always a form of desecration."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7be3ffef-b982-31a5-9a20-72788109ef91",
                                        "entry_id": "9bcf4a61-6ac6-3636-80e3-15d0431a86ed",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A challenge to a widely held belief, tradition or cherished institution."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
